Magic Progression

Purpose

Magic is an independent progression system that exists alongside technological development.

Magic should provide unique resources, mechanics, crafting systems, rituals, exploration, and progression paths that cannot simply be replaced by industrial technology.

Magic should complement technology without becoming a shortcut through the main industrial progression.

Magic Philosophy

Magic should feel fundamentally different from industrial technology.

Technology focuses on:

Machines

Power

Automation

Processing

Engineering

Infrastructure

Magic focuses on:

Rituals

Arcane resources

Magical crafting

Exploration

Knowledge

Specialized abilities

Magical infrastructure

Neither system should completely replace the other.

Magic Progression

Magic should have its own progression structure.

The progression should begin with accessible magical systems and gradually introduce increasingly powerful mechanics.

Early magic should require exploration, experimentation, and basic magical resources.

Advanced magic should require rare resources, complex rituals, specialized infrastructure, and progression through multiple magical systems.

Starting Magic

The first magical progression should become available after the player has established a stable survival foundation.

Early magic should introduce:

Basic magical resources

Magical crafting

Basic rituals

Arcane mechanics

Early exploration

The player should learn the fundamental rules of the magical progression before accessing advanced systems.

Magical Resources

Magic should introduce resources that are distinct from normal industrial materials.

These may include:

Arcane materials

Magical essences

Rare crystals

Ritual components

Magical plants

Mob-derived resources

Exploration-based resources

Magical resources should have meaningful uses throughout the progression.

Advanced magical resources should require increasingly difficult methods of acquisition.

Magical Machines

Magical machines and infrastructure should become available as magical progression advances.

They may provide:

Resource processing

Magical energy generation

Specialized crafting

Ritual automation

Magical storage

Resource transformation

Magical utility systems

Magical machines should not simply duplicate industrial machines.

They should provide unique capabilities that justify their existence.

Rituals

Rituals should be an important part of advanced magical progression.

Rituals should require:

Specific materials

Specific structures

Magical resources

Preparation

Knowledge

Appropriate progression

Advanced rituals may require resources or infrastructure from multiple magical systems.

Rituals should remain meaningfully different from ordinary crafting.

Magical Progression Tiers

Magic should have multiple progression stages.

Early Magic

Introduces basic magical systems and resources.

Intermediate Magic

Introduces advanced crafting, stronger magical resources, and more complex systems.

Advanced Magic

Introduces powerful rituals, rare resources, advanced magical machines, and major exploration requirements.

Endgame Magic

Introduces the most powerful magical systems and cross-mod interactions.

The exact tier structure will be defined after the main magic mods are selected.

Exploration Integration

Exploration should be an important part of magical progression.

Certain magical resources may require:

Specific biomes

Structures

Dimensions

Bosses

Rare mobs

Exploration objectives

The player should not be able to obtain every magical resource by remaining inside a single base.

Exploration should remain relevant even in the late game.

Technology Integration

Magic and technology should interact without becoming identical systems.

Industrial infrastructure may be required to support advanced magical production.

Examples include:

Industrial processing of magical materials

Advanced machines producing ritual components

AE2 networks managing magical resources

Create infrastructure transporting magical materials

High-tier industrial materials used in magical crafting

These integrations should be introduced at appropriate progression stages.

Magic should not bypass the technological tiers.

Magical resources should not provide unrestricted access to advanced industrial materials.

Magical Automation

Magic may eventually become partially or heavily automated.

Early magic should require significant manual interaction.

Intermediate magic may introduce limited automation.

Advanced magic may allow automated resource processing and ritual infrastructure.

Endgame magic may support large-scale automated magical production.

Automation should require substantial magical infrastructure.

Cross-Mod Magical Recipes

Advanced magical recipes may require materials from technology mods.

Possible requirements include:

GregTech materials

Modern Industrialization components

Mekanism materials

Create components

AE2 components

Exploration resources

Magical resources

Cross-mod recipes should be used to create meaningful connections between magic and technology.

They should not exist solely to increase recipe difficulty.

Magic and GregTech

GregTech remains the primary industrial progression.

Magic may provide specialized resources or systems that interact with GregTech.

GregTech materials may also be required for advanced magical infrastructure.

Neither system should completely replace the other.

Magic and Create

Create may provide mechanical infrastructure for magical systems.

Mechanical transportation, automation, and physical infrastructure may be used to support magical production.

Magic should still retain unique mechanics that cannot be reproduced by Create.

Magic and Mekanism

Mekanism may provide chemical processing or specialized industrial support for magical systems.

Advanced magical materials may require industrial processing before they can be used.

Magic should not bypass Mekanism's progression.

Magic and AE2

AE2 may become the primary logistics system for advanced magical factories.

Large magical production networks may eventually use digital storage and automated crafting.

AE2 should automate logistics rather than remove magical progression requirements.

Magical Equipment

Magical equipment should follow the magical progression.

Powerful equipment should require appropriate magical resources, crafting systems, exploration, or rituals.

Equipment should not provide unrestricted access to areas or materials that are intended to require technological progression.

Magical Bosses

Powerful magical bosses may act as progression gates.

Bosses may provide:

Rare materials

Unique components

Magical resources

Progression items

Access to advanced magical systems

Boss progression should be integrated with the overall progression of the pack.

Magic Quests

Magic should have dedicated quest chapters.

Quests should introduce:

Basic magical systems

Magical resources

Rituals

Magical machines

Exploration

Advanced magic

Magical automation

Endgame magic

The quest system should explain the progression without removing the need for experimentation.

GuideME Integration

GuideME should contain detailed documentation for the magical systems.

Documentation should explain:

Magical resources

Machines

Rituals

Progression requirements

Exploration requirements

Magical energy systems

Cross-mod interactions

Endgame systems

The quest system should guide the player while GuideME provides detailed reference information.

Magical Endgame

The magical endgame should provide powerful systems that remain relevant after the main technological progression is completed.

Endgame magic may include:

Extreme rituals

Rare magical resources

Powerful magical equipment

Advanced magical automation

Unique magical structures

Cross-mod magical systems

Magical progression should continue to provide meaningful objectives during the post-endgame.

Progression Integrity

Magic must not provide unintended shortcuts through the main progression.

Magical systems must not provide early access to:

High-tier industrial materials

High-tier machines

Advanced power systems

Endgame resources

ProjectE

Avaritia

Any other final progression systems

Magic should remain a complementary progression path rather than an alternative route that invalidates industrial development.

Final Goal

Magic should feel like a complete progression system with its own identity, resources, mechanics, exploration, infrastructure, and endgame.

Technology and magic should eventually become capable of interacting at extremely high levels without becoming interchangeable.

The player should be able to build an industrial civilization and a magical infrastructure that depend on each other while remaining fundamentally different systems.
